109 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 92 0 R
/T (Email Phishing The most common type. Attackers send fake emails pretending to be trusted companies like banks, Amazon, or Netflix. These emails often create urgency, asking you to "verify your account" or "update payment info" through malicious links.)
/E (Email Phishing The most common type. Attackers send fake emails pretending to be trusted companies like banks, Amazon, or Netflix. These emails often create urgency, asking you to "verify your account" or "update payment info" through malicious links.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
110 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 92 0 R
/T (Spear Phishing A targeted attack aimed at specific individuals. Attackers research their victims using social media and company websites to craft personalized messages. These are harder to detect because they reference real details about you or your workplace.)
/E (Spear Phishing A targeted attack aimed at specific individuals. Attackers research their victims using social media and company websites to craft personalized messages. These are harder to detect because they reference real details about you or your workplace.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
